  "result": "I added `click.KeyValue` and it works as `@click.option('--set', type=click.KeyValue())`. The full test suite passes, including a new test for it.\n\n- **Parsing:** it splits on the first `=`, so `a=b=c` gives `('a', 'b=c')`. An empty value is allowed, so `a=` gives `('a', '')`.\n- **Errors:** input with no `=` or with an empty key (`abc`, `=v`, an empty string) fails with `'abc' is not a valid key=value pair.` and exit code 2.\n- **Already-parsed input:** a tuple passed in directly is returned as `(key, value)` without re-parsing.\n- **Where it lives:** the class is in `src/click/types.py` and is exported from `src/click/__init__.py`. I also added it to `docs/api.md`.\n- **Test:** `test_key_value` is in `tests/test_types.py`.",
